    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nStarter\n\n### Description\n\nAt present, the 1-based indexing means that one needs two keystrokes to access the first file in the recent file list if there are more than 10 files listed, since multiple files will start with 1 in the index. If 0-based indexing is available, one can access the first file in the list with just one keystroke since only that file starts with 0 in the index, which is going to be more convenient.",
